Sval: no Firefox View or Restore Previous Session in the menu bar

Sval's workspaces replace Firefox's tab notions: Firefox View is closed,
and Sval restores from its tree (spec §10.4). The menu bar markup is
included in every macOS window, the hidden window among them, which shows
its menu bar when no other window is open. The hidden window is created
before `final-ui-startup` (`XREMain::XRE_mainRun`), earlier than Sval's
startup code and outside the browser-window hooks, so the items start
hidden in the markup. macOS reads only `hidden` when it draws the menu bar
(`nsMenuUtilsX::NodeIsHiddenOrCollapsed`), and nothing in Firefox shows
either item again.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml b/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml
